Feature: Actions through the relay agent and the broker
  Every scenario runs in the 6 cells of TL-7, under the network profiles its tags name.
  In every cell, sshd is off in the guest after acquisition and before the first action.

  @AC-55 @TL-7 @N0 @N1 @N2 @N3
  Scenario: An action runs in the desktop session
    Given a lease whose relay agent has registered with the broker
    When the client runs an action on a macOS target
    Then the action reads a test item from the login keychain without unlocking it
    And the action drives Finder with osascript without a consent dialog and without a TCC grant for sshd-keygen-wrapper
    And the action captures the screen through cua-driver
    When the client runs an action on an Ubuntu target
    Then the action sees the desktop session's display and session bus
    And the action reads a test item from the login keyring

  @AC-56 @TL-7 @N0 @N1 @N2 @N3
  Scenario: A command behaves as it would in a terminal of the desktop session
    When the client runs commands that exit with the statuses 0, 1 and 127
    Then the client receives each exit status exactly
    When the client sends 1 MiB on standard input to a command that prints its SHA-256
    Then the printed hash matches the sent bytes
    When a command that starts child processes exceeds its timeout or is cancelled
    Then every process of its process group has exited

  @AC-57 @TL-7 @N0 @N1 @N2 @N3
  Scenario: Large output arrives whole
    When the client runs a command that writes 200 MB to standard output and 1 MB to standard error
    Then the client receives both streams with the SHA-256 that the command computed

  @AC-58 @TL-7 @N0 @N1 @N2 @N3
  Scenario: Files move whole or not at all
    When the client pushes and pulls a 1 KiB file, a 2 GB file and a tree of 10,000 files
    Then every file arrives with its SHA-256
    And no reader in the guest ever sees a partly written file

  @AC-59 @TL-7 @N0 @N1 @N2 @N3
  Scenario: A long action completes
    When the client runs an action that works for 30 minutes and prints a line every minute
    Then the client receives every line and the action's exit status

  @AC-60 @TL-7 @N0 @N1 @N2 @N3
  Scenario: A lease's relay agent registers and its credential ends at release
    When the client acquires a lease
    Then the lease reaches running only after its relay agent has registered within its bound
    When the client releases the lease
    Then the broker refuses the lease credential and the agent credential

  @AC-61 @TL-7 @N1 @N2 @N3
  Scenario: A connection cut during an action does not run it twice
    Given an action in flight that appends one line to a file
    When the rig resets the client's connection and the relay agent's connection
    Then both sides resume their sessions
    And the client receives the action's result once
    And the file holds one line

  @AC-62 @TL-7 @N1 @N2 @N3
  Scenario: A silent connection is detected and resumed
    Given an action in flight
    When the rig blackholes the connection without closing it
    Then the dead connection is detected within 15 seconds
    And the session resumes and the result arrives once

  @AC-63 @TL-7 @N1 @N2 @N3
  Scenario: A client that changes its address keeps its session
    Given an action in flight
    When the client reconnects from a new source address and port
    Then the broker resumes the same session and the result arrives once

  @AC-64 @TL-7 @N1 @N2 @N3
  Scenario: A restart of the broker or the relay agent never replays an action
    Given an action in flight
    When the broker restarts, or the relay agent restarts
    Then each side reconnects
    And the action is reported completed, running or unknown, and is never run again

  @AC-65 @TL-7 @N1 @N2 @N3
  Scenario: The relay agent returns after a reboot
    When the guest reboots
    Then the relay agent registers again from the desktop session without a manual step
    And AC-55 passes again

  @AC-66 @TL-7 @N0 @N1 @N2 @N3
  Scenario: Credentials and ports are guarded
    Then the broker refuses a missing, wrong, expired or released credential
    And the target has no listening port that the relay agent opened
    And every hop of the chain runs TLS
    And the credentials work when a proxy ends TLS on the way

  @AC-67 @TL-7 @N1 @N2 @N3
  Scenario: An expired session still reports its operations
    Given a session with a grace period of 2 seconds and an action in flight
    When the client stays disconnected for 3 seconds and then resumes
    Then the client is answered expired
    And a query by execution ID returns the action's outcome

  @AC-68 @TL-7 @N0 @N1 @N2 @N3
  Scenario: The client finds the broker by name
    When the client looks up the instance through discovery
    Then it receives a relay_url that names a host name
    And the client connects without any address that a person wrote down

  @AC-69 @TL-7 @N1 @N2 @N3
  Scenario: A silent action survives the edge's idle close
    When the client runs an action that prints nothing for 5 minutes and then exits
    Then the session stays open through heartbeats
    And the client receives the exit status

  @AC-70 @TL-7 @N0 @N2
  Scenario: The link is the smallest part of an action's time
    When the client runs 100 short actions
    Then the suite records the time each action spent in the link and in the guest
    And it reports the median and the 95th percentile for each cell
